@model Student
@* LAB 18 — Lab ID: 31 | CHIP_YEAR = 4 | CHIP_LABEL = Final *@
@* 
    Question: why does Model mean one Student in this file and a whole List<Student> in Index.cshtml?
    Answer: Because of the @model directive at the top of each file. Index.cshtml declares @model List<Student> which makes its Model property a list collection, while _StudentRow.cshtml declares @model Student which makes its Model property a single student object.
*@

@*
WHAT THE BROWSER RECEIVED:
<span class="badge bg-warning text-dark" title="rendered by saif">Final</span>

SYMPTOMS OF BROKEN STATES:
- (a) Removing @addTagHelper from _ViewImports.cshtml:
  Symptom: The browser receives the literal custom tag `<year-chip for="4"></year-chip>` in the HTML page source, which renders as empty text on the screen because the browser does not recognize custom tag elements.
- (b) Removing output.TagMode = TagMode.StartTagAndEndTag from YearChipTagHelper.cs:
  Symptom: The browser receives a self-closing span tag `<span class="badge bg-warning text-dark" title="rendered by saif" />` without an end tag, rendering as an empty, invisible badge containing no visible text.
- (c) Renaming element to yearchip (no hyphen) in YearChipTagHelper.cs and in _StudentRow.cshtml:
  Symptom: The browser receives the custom tag `<yearchip for="4"></yearchip>` as literal HTML and displays nothing, because Razor fails to recognize the tag as a Tag Helper without the hyphen and bypasses processing.

What all three failures have in common:
All three failures fail silently and invisibly at compile time and run time (no exceptions are thrown), outputting invalid or unrecognized HTML tags directly to the browser.
*@

